<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Vereeniging</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1902</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Vereeniging, signed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pretoria">Pretoria</a> on 31 May 1902, ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a>. The South African Republic and the Orange Free State accepted British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a> Colony and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orange-river-colony">Orange River Colony</a>, in exchange for promised self-government, reconstruction funds and the deferral of any decision on votes for black Africans. The two colonies joined the Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> in 1910.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-vereeniging.jpg" alt="Treaty of Vereeniging" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AmandaCalitz · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Table_where_treaty_was_signed.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
